Apply this domain algorithm to prepared evidence: Analyze repeated fit problems to identify structural defects. Separate insufficient annotation guidance from real conceptual change, inspect negative examples, and avoid proliferating categories for every rare wording variant.
For each field, return a value only when supported, source IDs, authority, one rejected alternative, and status established, disputed, unknown, or inapplicable. Preserve contrary evidence and distinguish observation from inference.
